Sam relates runtime clients, business logic, infrastructure policies, and deployed resources in [one typed program](/lore/cafe-stack).
The compiler can check these relationships before deployment.

## Contract → surfaces

A [contract](/lore/one-capability-every-surface) defines shared input, output, failures, and metadata.
Projections turn registered capabilities into command line, HTTP, MCP tools, browser RPC, and code mode surfaces.
Each surface derives its input and failure definitions from the same schemas.

## Code → bindings → resources

A client operation can imply a policy requirement supplied when the function is built.
Sam describes [bindings](/lore/bindings) as permissions and environment variables together at [37:09](https://youtu.be/YEn4A7XxgF4?t=2229).
An Alchemy Layer can declare the cloud resources behind a service.
The [Stack](/lore/effect-office-hours-27-alchemy-infrastructure-as-effects) declares cloud resources.

## Plan → review → deploy

A [plan model](/lore/plan-model) describes infrastructure changes before they apply.
Sam connects Effect purity with a reviewable plan and a concrete deployment result at [12:22](https://youtu.be/YEn4A7XxgF4?t=742).
Tests using real infrastructure check behavior after deployment at [16:01](https://youtu.be/fPSxB7ZgSJw?t=961).

## The compiler checks the joins

[Effect](/lore/context-and-requirements) tracks required services in its type.
Effects and Layers let the type system track the resource providers a Stack needs at [07:01](https://youtu.be/fPSxB7ZgSJw?t=421).
Sam describes a type error when code still requires a removed binding at [15:25](https://youtu.be/YEn4A7XxgF4?t=925).
The compiler can check these relationships before deployment: [Happy Path 116, 28:00](https://youtu.be/YEn4A7XxgF4?t=1680).

## Cartridges

A [cartridge](/lore/cartridges) is a package that owns one job and the resources it needs.
Replacing its Layer changes the implementation and dependencies without changing callers.

## Lifecycles

Use an [XState machine](/lore/lifecycles-are-machines) for named states, retries, cancellation, or a lifecycle to resume or inspect.
Model the states and the events that move between them.

## The fence

The [fence](/lore/the-fence) is the compiler checks, lint rules, tests, and hooks that enforce project rules.
These rules cannot establish whole-program behavior.

## Cloud as a library

Sam's phrase is that [the whole cloud becomes a library](/lore/cloud-as-a-library), at [29:50](https://youtu.be/MtKHzAH6uXM?t=1790).
He argues that infrastructure tools can retain application-code properties such as debugging and tests at [03:50](https://youtu.be/YEn4A7XxgF4?t=230).

## The joins at a glance

- **Contract → surfaces**:
  - What the program checks: Shared input and failure schemas
  - Where to read more: [One capability, every surface](/lore/one-capability-every-surface)
- **Code → bindings → resources**:
  - What the program checks: Required services and resource providers
  - Where to read more: [Bindings](/lore/bindings) · [Infrastructure as Effects, Office Hours 27](/lore/effect-office-hours-27-alchemy-infrastructure-as-effects)
- **Plan → review → deploy**:
  - What the program checks: Changes before application; real-infrastructure behavior after deployment
  - Where to read more: [Plan model](/lore/plan-model)
- **Compiler → joins**:
  - What the program checks: Relationships before deployment; code that requires a removed binding
  - Where to read more: [Happy Path 116](/lore/happy-path-116-infrastructure-as-effects-sam-goodwin)
- **Cartridges**:
  - What the program checks: Removal leaves no loose resources or broken imports
  - Where to read more: [Cartridges](/lore/cartridges)
- **Lifecycles**:
  - What the program checks: Named states and the events between them
  - Where to read more: [Lifecycles are machines](/lore/lifecycles-are-machines)
- **Fence**:
  - What the program checks: Project rules; whole-program behavior remains outside these checks
  - Where to read more: [The fence](/lore/the-fence)
- **Cloud as a library**:
  - What the program checks: Debugging and tests for infrastructure code
  - Where to read more: [Cloud as a library](/lore/cloud-as-a-library)
